From 3fddef1bf074996b1b4d72f13f86f63e21c5dfa0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 23:05:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10212/11362] Seven test suites pinned to null; two
 stale-live-state fixtures repaired

Companion to f5f4364cc6 (writers) and a33755953d (artifacts), per
REQ-CONDUCTOR-VERDICT-3. Each suite now asserts the finished run
declares verdict_class null, and each validator's partial-rejection
rule carries a dedicated mutation case (specific error message, so a
checksum mismatch cannot shadow it; exp6687's case recomputes the
checksum for exactly that reason).

Two suites depended on live mutable state and had been failing or
erroring for reasons unrelated to any code change:
- test_experiment_6687: its fixture required the ACTIVE roadmap to
  still be V582, so 15 of 17 tests errored at setup once V583
  activated. The archived V582 manifest (commit a8e0d917e5) is now
  pinned in the fixture.
- test_experiment_6526: gate contracts checked field spelling against
  the LIVE roadmap, so all 7 failed once V565 activated (reproduced
  byte-identically in a pre-change worktree at e187fc8a31). The V564
  gate declarations (commit 73cef259c4) are now pinned.

openspec/capabilities/capstone/spec.md: REQ-CAPSTONE-6526's
verdict_class principle amended (dated, append-style) to match the
corrected writer semantics; the spec test asserts the texts agree.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
